  "slug": "decoding-codes-88bf",
  "summary": "New decoders such as SCOPE, TEMPO-BP and TCBP-JOBS target qLDPC accuracy under real-time latency, alongside circuit-scheduling and code-design advances.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is decoding quantum LDPC codes accurately within real-time budgets. SCOPE, a physics-informed parallel decoder, reports a logical error rate of 4.82e-10 on the [[144,12,12]] bivariate bicycle code with 173.8 ns latency. TEMPO-BP adapts per-variable memory strength through local feedback, outperforming BP+OSD and Relay-BP. TCBP-JOBS learns calibrated fault probabilities on GPUs and matches Tesseract accuracy. A hybrid sliding-window decoder for trapped-ion noise uses soft-output confidence to switch windows, improving on BP-LSD. For surface codes, Beyond Blossom reports a 4.23x geometric-mean speedup for CPU MWPM via local predecoding. A second strand targets syndrome-extraction circuits: Proxima schedules them using a DEM-based proximity metric, and structure-guided CP-SAT synthesis lowers logical error rates for CSS qLDPC codes. Code-design work adds Armillary codes with rates above 1/2 for fixed-connectivity superconducting hardware and rate-optimal distance-3 and distance-4 color codes simulated at break-even.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
